    "urlSlug": "/wood-fence/",
    "cleanSlug": "wood-fence",
    "content": "<h1>Wood Fence Installation in Rochester, NY</h1>\n\n<p>Wood remains the most popular fence material in the Rochester area, and for good reason. It looks warm and natural, it works with almost any house style, and it can be built in many designs, from tall solid privacy panels to charming picket fences. Xotix Fence provides wood fence installation for homeowners across Rochester and Monroe County, with careful construction designed for our freeze and thaw winters.</p>\n\n<h2>Cedar or Pressure-Treated Wood</h2>\n\n<p>Two types of wood dominate the local market. Cedar is naturally resistant to rot and insects, has an attractive grain and weathers to a soft silver if left unstained. It is a premium option for homeowners who want beauty and good longevity. Pressure-treated lumber is infused with preservatives to resist decay and is typically more economical, making it a practical choice for longer runs and budget-minded projects. The <a href=\"https://www.fpl.fs.usda.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">U.S. Forest Products Laboratory</a> publishes research on wood durability if you want to understand how different species and treatments hold up.</p>\n\n<p>Either choice can perform well when the fence is installed correctly and maintained. We will explain the tradeoffs for your property, your budget and how long you want the fence to look its best.</p>\n\n<h2>Popular Wood Fence Styles</h2>\n\n<p>Wood is flexible, which is why homeowners can match the style to their goal. Solid board <a href=\"/privacy-fence/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">privacy fence</a>s block sightlines and noise. Shadowbox fences alternate boards on each side so air passes through while still offering good privacy. Stockade fences use close-set pickets for a traditional look. Picket fences add curb appeal to front yards. Dog-ear tops give a finished, classic edge, and split rail fences suit large rural lots where you want a boundary rather than a barrier.</p>\n\n<h2>Why Installation Quality Matters</h2>\n\n<p>Wood fences fail early for one main reason: poor installation. When posts are too shallow, concrete is skimped, or boards sit directly on wet soil, moisture and frost go to work. In our climate, posts need to reach below the frost line, boards should stay slightly off the ground, and fasteners should be corrosion-resistant. Gates need sturdy framing so they do not sag.</p>\n\n<p>We build with these details in mind, with posts set deep and aligned, rails secured and boards fastened evenly. The goal is a fence that looks crisp on the first day and still looks straight years later.</p>\n\n<h2>Staining, Sealing and Maintenance</h2>\n\n<p>Wood is a natural material, so it benefits from care. New lumber often needs time to dry before staining or sealing, and a protective finish helps limit moisture damage, fading and cracking. Plan to inspect your fence each spring after winter, tighten any loose fasteners, trim plants away from boards and refresh the finish as needed. A little maintenance goes a long way.</p>\n\n<p>If you prefer a low-maintenance alternative, our <a href=\"/vinyl-fence/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">vinyl fence installation</a> service offers a similar privacy look without staining or painting.</p>\n\n<h2>When to Choose Wood</h2>\n\n<p>Wood is a great fit if you want a traditional appearance, need a custom height or design, want the option to paint or stain to match your home, or prefer a lower upfront cost than some other materials. It is especially popular for backyard privacy, garden enclosures, dog runs and decks.</p>\n\n<p>If you already have a wood fence that is leaning or rotting, we can tell you whether targeted <a href=\"/fence-repair/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">fence repair</a> makes sense or whether replacement is the smarter investment.</p>\n\n<h2>Common Questions About Wood Fences</h2>\n\n<p><strong>How long does a wood fence last in Rochester?</strong> Lifespan depends on the wood, installation and upkeep. Well-built fences that are sealed and maintained generally last many years, while neglected or shallow-set fences wear out sooner.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Should I stain right away?</strong> Pressure-treated wood often needs time to dry first. We can advise you on timing for your material.</p>\n\n<p><strong>How tall can my fence be?</strong> Height limits vary by municipality and location on the lot, so check local rules before choosing a design.</p>\n\n<h2>How a Xotix Fence project works</h2>\n\n<p>Every project follows the same clear path so you always know what happens next.</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Estimate and walk-through. We review your property, discuss what you want the fence to do, measure the run, and note gates, slopes, trees and obstacles. We bring sample styles and discuss board type, post caps and finishing details.</li>\n<li>Property lines and utilities. Before any digging, the fence line is confirmed against your survey or known markers, and underground utilities are marked through the 811 process.</li>\n<li>Permits and approvals. Many Monroe County municipalities and some neighborhoods have rules on height, setbacks and style. We help you understand what applies so there are no surprises.</li>\n<li>Installation. Posts are set below the local frost line, rails and panels are aligned and fastened, and gates are hung and adjusted so they swing and latch properly.</li>\n<li>Final walk-through. We check the finished fence with you, clean up the work area, and explain simple care steps so it keeps its good looks for years.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Where We Build Wood Fences</h2>\n\n<p>Xotix Fence serves homeowners and businesses across Rochester and surrounding Monroe County communities, including Greece, Irondequoit, Brighton, Henrietta, Gates, Chili, Penfield, Webster, Fairport, Pittsford, Victor and Spencerport.</p>\n\n<h2>Request your wood fence estimate</h2>\n\n<p>Ready to get started? Contact Xotix Fence Installation Rochester at <a href=\"tel:+15854818674\">+15854818674</a> or visit us at 264 Hudson Ave, Rochester, NY 14605, United States to talk through your project. Tell us your address, the type of fence you have in mind, and any deadlines you are working toward, and we will follow up with the next steps. Clear scope, honest recommendations and tidy workmanship are what we aim to deliver on every job.</p>",
