    "seoTitle": "Chain Link Fence Installation Rochester NY | Xotix Fence",
    "metaDescription": "Chain link fence installation in Rochester, NY. Galvanized and black vinyl-coated fences for homes, dog runs and businesses. Request an estimate.",
    "urlSlug": "/chain-link-fence/",
    "cleanSlug": "chain-link-fence",
    "content": "<h1>Chain Link Fence Installation in Rochester, NY</h1>\n\n<p>Chain link is the workhorse of the fencing world. It is strong, practical, quick to install and one of the most cost-effective ways to enclose a yard, a dog run, a play area or a commercial property. Xotix Fence provides chain link fence installation across Rochester and Monroe County for homeowners, landlords, schools and businesses that need dependable fencing without unnecessary extras.</p>\n\n<h2>Why Choose Chain Link</h2>\n\n<p>Chain link earns its popularity through value and durability. The steel mesh stands up to weather, handles heavy use and lasts a long time when properly installed. It lets sunlight and airflow through, which is helpful in gardens and along open yards, and it keeps pets and children contained while preserving the view. For long runs and large areas, it is often the most economical fencing choice.</p>\n\n<p>It is also easy to adapt. Gates can be added at almost any point (see our <a href=\"/fence-gates/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">fence gates</a> page for options), heights can be tailored, and privacy slats can be woven in later if you decide you want more coverage.</p>\n\n<h2>Galvanized and Black Vinyl-Coated Options</h2>\n\n<p>Two finishes are especially common. Galvanized chain link has a zinc coating that protects the steel from rust and gives the classic silver look. Black or green vinyl-coated chain link adds a polymer layer over the galvanized wire, which blends into landscaping and gives a more finished appearance. Black chain link has become a favorite for residential yards because it nearly disappears against trees and shrubs while still delivering strength.</p>\n\n<p>The <a href=\"https://www.chainlinkinfo.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">Chain Link Fence Manufacturers Institute</a> publishes helpful reference material on fabric, coatings and specifications if you want to learn more about how products are graded.</p>\n\n<h2>Residential Chain Link Fences</h2>\n\n<p>At home, chain link works well for backyards, side yards, dog runs, garden enclosures, and swimming pool perimeters where local code allows. Many homeowners choose it to give kids and pets room to roam without spending as much as they would on privacy fencing. If you later want more seclusion, privacy slats or a switch to a different style are always options, and you can explore the benefits of a <a href=\"/privacy-fence/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">privacy fence</a> on our dedicated page.</p>\n\n<h2>Commercial Chain Link Fences</h2>\n\n<p>Businesses depend on chain link for perimeter security, storage yards, parking lots, utility sites, ball fields, schools and apartment complexes. Heavy-gauge fabric, stronger posts, barbed or security top options and rolling or swing gates can all be specified for demanding sites. See our <a href=\"/commercial-fencing/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">commercial fencing</a> page for more about larger-scale projects.</p>\n\n<h2>Installation Details That Matter</h2>\n\n<p>Chain link looks simple, but quality depends on detail. Terminal posts at corners, ends and gates carry the tension of the fabric, so they must be set deeply and braced correctly. Line posts need even spacing and proper depth below the frost line. The fabric must be stretched evenly and secured so it does not sag. Top rails, tension wire, fittings and gate frames all need to be matched to the job.</p>\n\n<p>In Rochester, frost heave and snow load are real concerns. We set posts with winter conditions in mind so the fence stays tight and level rather than leaning after a few seasons.</p>\n\n<h2>Chain Link Heights and Gauges</h2>\n\n<p>Residential fences are commonly four feet tall, with five and six foot options for pets, security or sports use. Fabric gauge affects strength and price, and heavier gauges are common in commercial applications. We will recommend a combination that matches your purpose and local height rules.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n\n<p><strong>Does chain link rust?</strong> Galvanized steel resists rust for many years, and vinyl-coated fabric adds another layer of protection.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Can I add privacy to chain link?</strong> Yes, privacy slats and screens can be added to many installations.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Is chain link allowed in my neighborhood?</strong> Some subdivisions or associations restrict it, especially in front yards, so check your local rules first.</p>\n\n<h2>How a Xotix Fence project works</h2>\n\n<p>Every project follows the same clear path so you always know what happens next.</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Estimate and walk-through. We review your property, discuss what you want the fence to do, measure the run, and note gates, slopes, trees and obstacles. We confirm the height, gate count, fabric style and any privacy options you would like.</li>\n<li>Property lines and utilities. Before any digging, the fence line is confirmed against your survey or known markers, and underground utilities are marked through the 811 process.</li>\n<li>Permits and approvals. Many Monroe County municipalities and some neighborhoods have rules on height, setbacks and style. We help you understand what applies so there are no surprises.</li>\n<li>Installation. Posts are set below the local frost line, rails and panels are aligned and fastened, and gates are hung and adjusted so they swing and latch properly.</li>\n<li>Final walk-through. We check the finished fence with you, clean up the work area, and explain simple care steps so it keeps its good looks for years.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Where We Install Chain Link</h2>\n\n<p>Xotix Fence serves homeowners and businesses across Rochester and surrounding Monroe County communities, including Greece, Irondequoit, Brighton, Henrietta, Gates, Chili, Penfield, Webster, Fairport, Pittsford, Victor and Spencerport.</p>\n\n<h2>Request your chain link fence estimate</h2>\n\n<p>Ready to get started? Contact Xotix Fence Installation Rochester at <a href=\"tel:+15854818674\">+15854818674</a> or visit us at 264 Hudson Ave, Rochester, NY 14605, United States to talk through your project. Tell us your address, the type of fence you have in mind, and any deadlines you are working toward, and we will follow up with the next steps. Clear scope, honest recommendations and tidy workmanship are what we aim to deliver on every job.</p>",
