    "seoTitle": "Aluminum Fence Installation Rochester NY | Ornamental",
    "metaDescription": "Aluminum and ornamental fence installation in Rochester, NY. Rust-free, elegant fencing for yards, pools and businesses. Request an estimate today.",
    "urlSlug": "/aluminum-fence/",
    "cleanSlug": "aluminum-fence",
    "content": "<h1>Aluminum Fence Installation in Rochester, NY</h1>\n\n<p>An aluminum fence gives your property a refined, finished look while providing dependable boundary protection. Unlike steel, aluminum does not rust, and its powder-coated finish stays attractive through rain, road salt, snow and sun. Xotix Fence installs aluminum and ornamental fencing for homeowners, builders and businesses throughout Rochester and Monroe County.</p>\n\n<h2>Why Aluminum Works Well in Rochester</h2>\n\n<p>Our region is rough on metal. Winter road salt, constant moisture and temperature swings can quickly corrode unprotected steel. Aluminum is naturally corrosion resistant, and a quality powder coat adds another protective layer. That makes it a smart pick for front yards, driveways and areas where salt spray is common. It is also lighter than steel, which helps with handling and installation.</p>\n\n<p>Aluminum is not as heavy-duty as steel in every application, so we match grade and picket thickness to the job. Residential systems are well suited to boundaries and pool enclosures, while commercial projects may call for heavier-duty panels.</p>\n\n<h2>Ornamental Styles and Finishes</h2>\n\n<p>Aluminum fencing comes in a wide range of looks. Flat-top designs are clean and modern. Spear-top and finial designs bring a classic wrought-iron feel without the upkeep. Picket spacing can be chosen for open views or tighter child and pet safety. Black remains the most popular color, though bronze, white and other finishes are available from many manufacturers. Decorative gates, arches and scrolls can add extra character at an entrance.</p>\n\n<h2>Pool Fencing and Safety</h2>\n\n<p>Aluminum is one of the most common choices for pool enclosures because it is durable, attractive and does not block the view. Pool barriers have to meet safety requirements, which typically include minimum heights and self-closing, self-latching gates. These rules can vary by municipality, so we recommend confirming local code. You can learn more on our <a href=\"/pool-fence/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">pool fence</a> page.</p>\n\n<h2>Open View, Strong Boundary</h2>\n\n<p>Many homeowners like aluminum because it defines a property without closing it in. You can keep your garden, home and landscaping visible while still creating a clear boundary and a safe space for pets. Unlike solid fences, aluminum also lets air and light through, which means it is less affected by wind loads.</p>\n\n<p>It is a good fit for front-yard boundaries, corner lots, pool areas, patios, school and church properties, and entrances to subdivisions and commercial sites.</p>\n\n<h2>Installation on Slopes and Uneven Ground</h2>\n\n<p>Many Rochester properties have grade changes. Aluminum fence panels can usually be racked to follow gentle slopes, while steeper areas may need stepped installation. Proper layout is important so panels remain level where intended and the line looks natural. We evaluate the grade during your estimate and plan the installation accordingly.</p>\n\n<h2>Gates and Hardware</h2>\n\n<p>Aluminum gates are available as single-swing, double-swing and driveway styles. Quality hinges, latches and gate posts are important for long-term performance. We can discuss lock options, self-closing hardware and automated gate openers where appropriate. Visit our <a href=\"/fence-gates/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">fence gates</a> page to learn more about gate options.</p>\n\n<h2>Care and Longevity</h2>\n\n<p>Aluminum needs very little maintenance. Rinse it occasionally to remove dirt and road salt residue, and touch up any scratches in the finish if needed. With basic care, a well-made aluminum fence can stay attractive for many years.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n\n<p><strong>Is aluminum fencing strong?</strong> Yes for residential and light commercial use, though it is lighter than steel.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Does aluminum provide privacy?</strong> Not by itself. For privacy, consider a <a href=\"/privacy-fence/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">privacy fence</a> in wood or vinyl, or add landscaping. For general product and installation background, the <a href=\"https://www.americanfenceassociation.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">American Fence Association</a> is a helpful resource.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Can I install it in winter?</strong> Often yes, depending on ground conditions, though frozen soil can affect scheduling.</p>\n\n<h2>How a Xotix Fence project works</h2>\n\n<p>Every project follows the same clear path so you always know what happens next.</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Estimate and walk-through. We review your property, discuss what you want the fence to do, measure the run, and note gates, slopes, trees and obstacles. We discuss panel height, picket style, finish color and gate locations here.</li>\n<li>Property lines and utilities. Before any digging, the fence line is confirmed against your survey or known markers, and underground utilities are marked through the 811 process.</li>\n<li>Permits and approvals. Many Monroe County municipalities and some neighborhoods have rules on height, setbacks and style. We help you understand what applies so there are no surprises.</li>\n<li>Installation. Posts are set below the local frost line, rails and panels are aligned and fastened, and gates are hung and adjusted so they swing and latch properly.</li>\n<li>Final walk-through. We check the finished fence with you, clean up the work area, and explain simple care steps so it keeps its good looks for years.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Where We Install Aluminum Fences</h2>\n\n<p>Xotix Fence serves homeowners and businesses across Rochester and surrounding Monroe County communities, including Greece, Irondequoit, Brighton, Henrietta, Gates, Chili, Penfield, Webster, Fairport, Pittsford, Victor and Spencerport.</p>\n\n<h2>Request your aluminum fence estimate</h2>\n\n<p>Ready to get started? Contact Xotix Fence Installation Rochester at <a href=\"tel:+15854818674\">+15854818674</a> or visit us at 264 Hudson Ave, Rochester, NY 14605, United States to talk through your project. Tell us your address, the type of fence you have in mind, and any deadlines you are working toward, and we will follow up with the next steps. Clear scope, honest recommendations and tidy workmanship are what we aim to deliver on every job.</p>",
