    "pageType": "Service",
    "pageTitle": "Privacy Fence Installation",
    "seoTitle": "Privacy Fence Installation Rochester NY | Xotix Fence",
    "metaDescription": "Privacy fence installation in Rochester, NY. Wood and vinyl privacy fences, including 6-foot designs, built for local winters. Request an estimate.",
    "urlSlug": "/privacy-fence/",
    "cleanSlug": "privacy-fence",
    "content": "<h1>Privacy Fence Installation in Rochester, NY</h1>\n\n<p>A privacy fence turns an exposed yard into a private outdoor room. Xotix Fence installs privacy fencing for homeowners across Rochester and Monroe County who want to enjoy their patios, pools, gardens and lawns without feeling watched. We build solid and semi-solid designs in wood and vinyl, with careful attention to height, layout and local rules.</p>\n\n<h2>What Makes a Fence a Privacy Fence</h2>\n\n<p>Privacy fences use closely spaced boards or solid panels that block views from neighbors, passersby and traffic. Most are between five and six feet tall, with six feet being the most requested height for backyards. Beyond sightlines, a good privacy fence reduces wind, softens street noise, hides trash bins and play equipment, and helps pets and children stay in the yard.</p>\n\n<h2>Wood or Vinyl Privacy Fencing</h2>\n\n<p>The right material depends on your preferences. Wood privacy fences offer a warm look and flexible design. You can choose cedar or pressure-treated boards, add lattice tops or decorative caps, and stain or paint to match your home. Read more about <a href=\"/wood-fence/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">wood fence installation</a> if that appeals to you. Vinyl privacy fences deliver a clean, uniform look with almost no upkeep, so there is no staining, no sanding and no painting. Our <a href=\"/vinyl-fence/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">vinyl fence installation</a> page explains the details of those systems.</p>\n\n<h2>Choosing the Right Height</h2>\n\n<p>Six-foot privacy fences are popular because they provide the most seclusion, but the best height depends on your yard and local code. Many municipalities limit front-yard fences to lower heights and permit taller fences only along side and rear lines. Corner lots often have extra restrictions near intersections for visibility. Check with your town, village or city first, and we will help you plan a layout that fits the rules.</p>\n\n<h2>Design Options</h2>\n\n<p>Privacy does not have to feel like a wall. Board-on-board designs overlap boards so there are no gaps even as wood shrinks. Shadowbox designs alternate boards on either side to allow airflow while still limiting views. Capped and lattice-topped fences add visual interest, and mixed-height designs can step down near the street. In vinyl, tongue-and-groove panels create a smooth, tight surface, while textured options mimic wood grain.</p>\n\n<h2>Wind, Snow and Rochester Conditions</h2>\n\n<p>Solid fences catch wind like a sail, so installation quality is especially important. Posts need to be deep enough, aligned correctly and set in solid material so the fence resists gusts and heavy snow. In our freeze and thaw climate, frost can also push shallow posts out of position. Using appropriate post spacing and depth is the best protection against leaning.</p>\n\n<p>Some homeowners choose semi-privacy designs with small gaps to reduce wind pressure while keeping most of the benefits.</p>\n\n<h2>Privacy for Pools, Patios and Pets</h2>\n\n<p>A privacy fence can also serve safety goals. If you have a swimming pool, check requirements for barriers and self-closing gates, and see our <a href=\"/pool-fence/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">pool fence</a> page. For dogs, make sure the fence is tall enough and that the bottom is secure against digging. We can add gates that work with your lawn equipment and daily routines.</p>\n\n<h2>Working With Neighbors and Property Lines</h2>\n\n<p>Before installing, know where your property line is. A survey or clear markers help avoid disputes. Talking with neighbors in advance is a courtesy, and the <a href=\"https://www.americanfenceassociation.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">American Fence Association</a> offers general consumer guidance on planning a project, and some people appreciate learning which side of the fence faces out. We recommend installing the finished side facing outward unless local rules say otherwise.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n\n<p><strong>How much does a 6-foot privacy fence cost?</strong> It depends on length, material, gates, terrain and removal of any old fence. We provide estimates based on your actual measurements.</p>\n\n<p><strong>How long does a privacy fence take?</strong> Many yards can be completed in a few days after materials and approvals are ready.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Do I need a permit?</strong> Often yes, depending on location. Confirm with your municipality.</p>\n\n<h2>How a Xotix Fence project works</h2>\n\n<p>Every project follows the same clear path so you always know what happens next.</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Estimate and walk-through. We review your property, discuss what you want the fence to do, measure the run, and note gates, slopes, trees and obstacles. This is when we talk about height, style, gate placement and which side of the fence will face out.</li>\n<li>Property lines and utilities. Before any digging, the fence line is confirmed against your survey or known markers, and underground utilities are marked through the 811 process.</li>\n<li>Permits and approvals. Many Monroe County municipalities and some neighborhoods have rules on height, setbacks and style. We help you understand what applies so there are no surprises.</li>\n<li>Installation. Posts are set below the local frost line, rails and panels are aligned and fastened, and gates are hung and adjusted so they swing and latch properly.</li>\n<li>Final walk-through. We check the finished fence with you, clean up the work area, and explain simple care steps so it keeps its good looks for years.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Where We Install Privacy Fences</h2>\n\n<p>Xotix Fence serves homeowners and businesses across Rochester and surrounding Monroe County communities, including Greece, Irondequoit, Brighton, Henrietta, Gates, Chili, Penfield, Webster, Fairport, Pittsford, Victor and Spencerport.</p>\n\n<h2>Request your privacy fence estimate</h2>\n\n<p>Ready to get started? Contact Xotix Fence Installation Rochester at <a href=\"tel:+15854818674\">+15854818674</a> or visit us at 264 Hudson Ave, Rochester, NY 14605, United States to talk through your project. Tell us your address, the type of fence you have in mind, and any deadlines you are working toward, and we will follow up with the next steps. Clear scope, honest recommendations and tidy workmanship are what we aim to deliver on every job.</p>",
