    "pageType": "Service",
    "pageTitle": "Fence Replacement",
    "seoTitle": "Fence Replacement Rochester NY | Old Fence Removal",
    "metaDescription": "Fence replacement in Rochester, NY. We remove worn-out fences and install new wood, vinyl, chain link or aluminum. Request an estimate.",
    "urlSlug": "/fence-replacement/",
    "cleanSlug": "fence-replacement",
    "content": "<h1>Fence Replacement in Rochester, NY</h1>\n\n<p>Every fence reaches the end of its life eventually. If yours leans, rots, sags or looks worn out, replacing it can restore your privacy, safety and curb appeal. Xotix Fence handles complete fence replacement for homeowners and businesses across Rochester and Monroe County, including tear-out of the old fence, site preparation and installation of a new one.</p>\n\n<h2>Signs It Is Time to Replace</h2>\n\n<p>Replacement makes sense when problems are widespread rather than isolated. Warning signs include multiple leaning or loose posts, rot at the base of posts and boards, large sections of broken or missing panels, gates that cannot be fixed, rust that has weakened chain link or hardware, and a fence that needs constant patching. If you find yourself calling for repairs every year, a new fence is often the more economical choice. For smaller issues, see our <a href=\"/fence-repair/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">fence repair</a> service first.</p>\n\n<h2>What Replacement Involves</h2>\n\n<p>Replacing a fence has more steps than building one on bare ground. We start by inspecting the existing line and confirming what must come out. Old panels, rails and posts are removed, and old concrete footings are dealt with so they do not interfere with the new layout. We then clear the line, check grade and drainage, and prepare to set new posts at the proper depth.</p>\n\n<p>Sometimes the new fence can follow the old line exactly. In other cases you may want to move it, change height, add gates or switch materials. This is a good time to rethink what you need.</p>\n\n<h2>Upgrading Your Material</h2>\n\n<p>Replacement is a chance to choose something that fits your life better. Homeowners who spent years staining wood often move to low-maintenance <a href=\"/vinyl-fence/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">vinyl fencing</a>. Others stay with wood for its look and choose cedar or higher-grade lumber this time. Some upgrade chain link to black vinyl-coated, or add an aluminum section at the front yard for a more refined appearance. Our <a href=\"/fence-installation/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">fence installation</a> page outlines the materials and what to expect from each.</p>\n\n<h2>Why Old Fences Fail Early</h2>\n\n<p>If your last fence only lasted a few years, the cause may not have been the material. Shallow posts, minimal concrete, poor drainage, untreated wood against wet soil and rushed layout are common culprits. A new fence should correct these issues. We set posts below the frost line, pay attention to water flow and use fasteners and hardware suited to Rochester conditions.</p>\n\n<h2>Property Lines, Permits and Neighbors</h2>\n\n<p>Before replacing, confirm where your property line actually is. Old fences are not always on the boundary, and moving a fence even a few inches can matter. Permit requirements may apply to replacements as well as new fences, especially if height or location changes. Also remember to arrange utility marking through <a href=\"https://www.call811.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">Call 811</a> before digging.</p>\n\n<p>If you share a fence with a neighbor, communicate early. Many people work out cost sharing or design preferences together, though that is a private matter between neighbors.</p>\n\n<h2>Disposal and Cleanup</h2>\n\n<p>Tearing out a fence creates a lot of debris. We include removal and cleanup in the scope of work, and we confirm details in your estimate. You can expect the site to be left tidy, with the new fence ready to use.</p>\n\n<h2>Timing Your Project</h2>\n\n<p>Spring and summer are busy, but many fence projects can also be done in fall and, depending on ground conditions, parts of winter. Scheduling early gives you more choice. If you want a fence ready before a graduation, pool season or new pet arrives, contact us ahead of time.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n\n<p><strong>Can I keep my old posts?</strong> Occasionally, if they are sound and properly placed, but most replacements use new posts.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Do you remove the old fence?</strong> Yes, tear-out and disposal can be included.</p>\n\n<p><strong>How long does replacement take?</strong> Usually longer than a repair but comparable to a new installation, depending on size.</p>\n\n<h2>How a Xotix Fence project works</h2>\n\n<p>Every project follows the same clear path so you always know what happens next.</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Estimate and walk-through. We review your property, discuss what you want the fence to do, measure the run, and note gates, slopes, trees and obstacles. We walk the existing fence line and decide what to reuse, remove or relocate.</li>\n<li>Property lines and utilities. Before any digging, the fence line is confirmed against your survey or known markers, and underground utilities are marked through the 811 process.</li>\n<li>Permits and approvals. Many Monroe County municipalities and some neighborhoods have rules on height, setbacks and style. We help you understand what applies so there are no surprises.</li>\n<li>Installation. Posts are set below the local frost line, rails and panels are aligned and fastened, and gates are hung and adjusted so they swing and latch properly.</li>\n<li>Final walk-through. We check the finished fence with you, clean up the work area, and explain simple care steps so it keeps its good looks for years.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Where We Replace Fences</h2>\n\n<p>Xotix Fence serves homeowners and businesses across Rochester and surrounding Monroe County communities, including Greece, Irondequoit, Brighton, Henrietta, Gates, Chili, Penfield, Webster, Fairport, Pittsford, Victor and Spencerport.</p>\n\n<h2>Request your fence replacement estimate</h2>\n\n<p>Ready to get started? Contact Xotix Fence Installation Rochester at <a href=\"tel:+15854818674\">+15854818674</a> or visit us at 264 Hudson Ave, Rochester, NY 14605, United States to talk through your project. Tell us your address, the type of fence you have in mind, and any deadlines you are working toward, and we will follow up with the next steps. Clear scope, honest recommendations and tidy workmanship are what we aim to deliver on every job.</p>",
