    "content": "<h1>Commercial Fencing in Rochester, NY</h1>\n\n<p>Businesses use fencing to protect people, property and inventory. A well-planned commercial fence controls access, reduces theft and liability, defines boundaries and gives customers a professional first impression. Xotix Fence installs commercial fencing and gates for Rochester and Monroe County businesses, property managers, schools, contractors and community organizations.</p>\n\n<h2>Where Commercial Fencing Is Used</h2>\n\n<p>Commercial properties have varied needs. Common projects include storage and equipment yards, parking lots and dealerships, warehouses and industrial sites, retail centers, apartment and townhome communities, schools and athletic fields, dumpster enclosures, utility sites and construction areas. Each demands a different mix of strength, appearance and access.</p>\n\n<h2>Commercial Fence Materials</h2>\n\n<p>Chain link is the most common commercial option because it is strong, economical and quick to install. Heavier gauge fabric, larger posts and commercial grade framing give it added durability. Our <a href=\"/chain-link-fence/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">chain link fence installation</a> page explains fabric and coating choices. Ornamental aluminum or steel fencing is a good choice where appearance matters, such as office entrances, apartments and medical properties. Wood or vinyl privacy fencing can screen dumpsters, mechanical equipment and loading areas. Barbed wire or security tops can be added to increase deterrence where permitted.</p>\n\n<h2>Security and Access Control</h2>\n\n<p>A fence is only as secure as its gates. Commercial properties often need wide swing gates, cantilever or sliding gates, heavy-duty hinges, lockable latches and compatibility with keypads, card readers or automatic operators. Safety and local code requirements should be considered, especially with automated gates. We can discuss options and coordinate with your electrical or security contractor when needed. For general gate planning, see our <a href=\"/fence-gates/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">fence gates</a> information.</p>\n\n<h2>Planning a Commercial Project</h2>\n\n<p>Commercial work benefits from careful planning. We look at property lines, site plans, traffic flow for trucks and customers, drainage, underground utilities, grade changes and visibility. Many commercial sites also have zoning rules, site-plan requirements, or lease provisions that affect what can be built. We encourage owners and property managers to check these early. If there is existing fencing, we can evaluate whether to expand it, repair it or replace it.</p>\n\n<h2>Built for Heavy Use</h2>\n\n<p>Commercial fences take more abuse than residential ones. Trucks bump gates, snow plows push against lines and gates open hundreds of times. We emphasize deep, well-set posts, braced corners, strong gate frames and durable hardware. In Rochester's freeze and thaw climate, proper footing depth is essential to keep long fence lines straight and gates functioning year after year.</p>\n\n<h2>Scheduling Around Your Business</h2>\n\n<p>Disruptions cost money. We coordinate access, work hours and phasing so your business can keep operating as much as possible. For larger sites, we can break a project into stages. Tell us about deadlines, inspections or insurance requirements and we will work with them.</p>\n\n<h2>Property Managers and Multi-Site Work</h2>\n\n<p>If you manage more than one property, consistent fencing helps maintain a uniform look and simplifies maintenance. We can help you standardize heights, styles and hardware across sites and handle ongoing repairs. Our <a href=\"/fence-repair/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">fence repair</a> service is available for existing commercial fences.</p>\n\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n\n<p><strong>How tall should a commercial fence be?</strong> Common heights range from six to eight feet, depending on use and local rules.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Can you match my existing fence?</strong> We can usually match style and height, though exact colors may vary. For independent industry background, the <a href=\"https://www.americanfenceassociation.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">American Fence Association</a> is a good starting point.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Do you handle gates with access control?</strong> We install gates and coordinate with specialists for electronics.</p>\n\n<h2>How a Xotix Fence project works</h2>\n\n<p>Every project follows the same clear path so you always know what happens next.</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Estimate and walk-through. We review your property, discuss what you want the fence to do, measure the run, and note gates, slopes, trees and obstacles. For commercial projects, we review site plans, access needs, security goals and schedule.</li>\n<li>Property lines and utilities. Before any digging, the fence line is confirmed against your survey or known markers, and underground utilities are marked through the 811 process.</li>\n<li>Permits and approvals. Many Monroe County municipalities and some neighborhoods have rules on height, setbacks and style. We help you understand what applies so there are no surprises.</li>\n<li>Installation. Posts are set below the local frost line, rails and panels are aligned and fastened, and gates are hung and adjusted so they swing and latch properly.</li>\n<li>Final walk-through. We check the finished fence with you, clean up the work area, and explain simple care steps so it keeps its good looks for years.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Where We Install Commercial Fencing</h2>\n\n<p>Xotix Fence serves homeowners and businesses across Rochester and surrounding Monroe County communities, including Greece, Irondequoit, Brighton, Henrietta, Gates, Chili, Penfield, Webster, Fairport, Pittsford, Victor and Spencerport.</p>\n\n<h2>Request your commercial fencing estimate</h2>\n\n<p>Ready to get started? Contact Xotix Fence Installation Rochester at <a href=\"tel:+15854818674\">+15854818674</a> or visit us at 264 Hudson Ave, Rochester, NY 14605, United States to talk through your project. Tell us your address, the type of fence you have in mind, and any deadlines you are working toward, and we will follow up with the next steps. Clear scope, honest recommendations and tidy workmanship are what we aim to deliver on every job.</p>",
