    "content": "<h1><a href=\"/fence-installation/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">Fence Installation</a> in Rochester, NY</h1>\n\n<p>Xotix Fence Installation Rochester is based around the city and the communities that surround it, so Rochester is where our work begins. From city neighborhoods with historic homes and narrow lots to busy commercial corridors, we install and repair fences that fit the property and handle the region's tough seasons. If you are looking for dependable fence installation in Rochester, NY, you are in the right place.</p>\n\n<h2>Fences for Rochester Homes and Properties</h2>\n\n<p>Rochester is a city of distinct neighborhoods. Areas such as Park Avenue, Browncroft, the 19th Ward, Highland Park, Charlotte, Corn Hill and Maplewood each have their own housing character, from early twentieth-century homes to later mid-century builds. Lots are often narrower than in the suburbs, with garages, driveways and alleys close to property lines, so careful measuring matters. A privacy fence in a tight backyard needs to respect setbacks, sit on the right side of the line and leave room for gates, utility access and maintenance. We pay close attention to these details so your fence adds value without creating problems.</p>\n\n<h2>Local Conditions We Plan For in Rochester</h2>\n\n<p>Rochester sits on the south shore of Lake Ontario and gets long winters, heavy snow and repeated freezing and thawing. Frost can push shallow posts out of alignment, and spring melt can leave soil soft. In older neighborhoods, mature tree roots, buried debris and old footings can complicate digging. We plan post depth below the frost line, look at drainage along the fence line and flag any obstacles before work begins, which helps avoid surprises and keeps the finished fence straight.</p>\n\n<h2>Most Requested Fences in Rochester</h2>\n\n<p>Rochester homeowners ask for a wide range of projects. Traditional <a href=\"/wood-fence/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">wood fence</a> designs are popular in older neighborhoods because they suit the character of the homes, and cedar privacy fences are common in backyards that back up to busy streets. Vinyl is a favorite for owners who want less upkeep, and chain link remains a practical choice for dog runs and rental properties. Many customers also need <a href=\"/fence-repair/\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">fence repair</a> after storms or years of neglect. Whatever your goal, we start with a measured plan and clear recommendations for your specific lot.</p>\n\n<h2>Permits and Local Rules in Rochester</h2>\n\n<p>Fence rules differ across Monroe County and neighboring areas, and they can cover maximum height, setbacks from the property line, front-yard restrictions, pool barrier requirements and how a fence must be finished. Before you build, confirm current requirements with the <a href=\"https://www.cityofrochester.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-lime-700 dark:text-lime-400 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white transition-colors\">City of Rochester</a>. Properties in the city are subject to City of Rochester rules, and nearby suburbs have their own. Historic districts may add review steps for style or materials. We help you understand what is likely to apply to your design, but the final answer always comes from your local code office.</p>\n\n<h2>Fence Services Available in Rochester</h2>\n\n<p>Xotix Fence offers the full range of fencing work to Rochester customers: new fence installation, wood, vinyl, chain link and aluminum fences, privacy fencing, pool fencing, gates, fence repair, fence replacement and commercial fencing. If you are not sure which material or style fits your property, we will compare the options for your lot, your budget and the way you use your yard, and we will give you a straightforward recommendation.</p>\n\n<h2>Planning Your Rochester Fence Project</h2>\n\n<p>The best time to plan a fence is before you need it. Spring and summer are the busiest seasons across the Rochester area, so reaching out early gives you more choice in scheduling and materials. Fall is often an excellent time to build, since the ground is workable and lead times can be shorter. During your estimate, we walk the proposed fence line with you, talk through height, style and gate locations, and point out anything specific to your Rochester property, such as slopes, trees, drainage or shared boundaries. You leave with a clear understanding of what will be built, how it will be built and what to expect along the way.</p>\n\n<h2>How a Xotix Fence project works</h2>\n\n<p>Every project follows the same clear path so you always know what happens next.</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li>Estimate and walk-through. We review your property, discuss what you want the fence to do, measure the run, and note gates, slopes, trees and obstacles. We also look at how Rochester lot layouts, trees and neighboring properties affect the fence line.</li>\n<li>Property lines and utilities. Before any digging, the fence line is confirmed against your survey or known markers, and underground utilities are marked through the 811 process.</li>\n<li>Permits and approvals. Many Monroe County municipalities and some neighborhoods have rules on height, setbacks and style. We help you understand what applies so there are no surprises.</li>\n<li>Installation. Posts are set below the local frost line, rails and panels are aligned and fastened, and gates are hung and adjusted so they swing and latch properly.</li>\n<li>Final walk-through. We check the finished fence with you, clean up the work area, and explain simple care steps so it keeps its good looks for years.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Rochester Fence Questions</h2>\n\n<p><strong>How do I know where my property line is in Rochester?</strong> A survey is the most reliable way. Old fences are not always on the line, so we recommend confirming before building.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Can you work on narrow city lots?</strong> Yes. We plan layout, gates and access carefully so the fence fits tight spaces.</p>\n\n<h2>Request your fence installation estimate</h2>\n\n<p>Ready to get started? Contact Xotix Fence Installation Rochester at <a href=\"tel:+15854818674\">+15854818674</a> or visit us at 264 Hudson Ave, Rochester, NY 14605, United States to talk through your project. Tell us your address, the type of fence you have in mind, and any deadlines you are working toward, and we will follow up with the next steps. Clear scope, honest recommendations and tidy workmanship are what we aim to deliver on every job.</p>",
